iginal), which standard each change served. Mid-unit assessment (day 18): the series plan, with a respond day. Out: a work about a culture's images and objects (unit 14). Tools: the series plan card, work cards, a reading on art and environmental memorials, Curio Class's own. Free path: any one medium the student has, paper. Short path: 17 days | After unit 12 because the series grows from the theme works and the reaction-over-time study; before unit 14 because the argument about a culture's images uses the series' research and the defended statement | Candidate: a series by a living maker from Africa or Asia aimed at a change in its community | Quick-to-See Smith's work answers the 1992 anniversary of Columbus's arrival: the sensitivity agent reads the National Gallery of Art's page and her own published words first; no student copies her imagery. The change a student plans is the student's choice from a checked list or invented; the side is never scored (values rule); a work on a sensitive subject is read by a second adult before it is shown (va-g11-design). Hazards and controls: per the medium chosen, from its hazard card; hands washed. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
